  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="8f64-02d6-e955-7d8d" name="Romano-British Civitates: Age of Vortigern (Age of Arthur) - List Notes" publicationId="28aa-c13e-b61d-4f3e" hidden="false">
      <description>ROMANO-BRITISH CIVITATES: AGE OF VORTIGERN (The Age of Arthur, pp.21-31). Units of Commanipulares, Milites (including Sagittari and Equites) and Pedyt may have a Leader (+5), Musician (+5) and Standard (+5). Allies are documented only.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Romano-British Civitates: Age of Vortigern]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Warriors: up to 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 25%
  AGE OF VORTIGERN (c.425-460). Characters up to 25% (no Dux/Comes). Common warriors up to 50% (Commanipulares, Pedyt). Uncommon up to 25% (Milites, Rustici). Allies up to 50% from one list: Scots-Irish (Ceithern led by Curadh or Toiseach), Saxons (Geoguth) or British and Welsh Kingdoms (Combrogi led by Tiern or Uchelwyr); Saxon allied units may have Leader, Standard and Musician free (documented). Advantages: Fabricae, Fearsome Blow, Finest Horses, Finest Armour, Knight Commander. Saint Germanus option: no allies, any number of points on Commanipulares and Pedyt.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
